# Alerting Patterns Guidelines

## Mục tiêu

Tài liệu này định nghĩa các nguyên tắc và best practices cho việc implement alerting systems trong Cursor Enterprise Framework. Mục tiêu là đảm bảo proactive issue detection, appropriate alerting thresholds, và effective incident response.

Alerting là phần critical của operational excellence, cho phép teams respond to issues trước khi customers notice. Việc implement alerting đúng cách reduce alert fatigue và ensures attention on real problems.

## Nguyên tắc cơ bản

### 1. Alert Severity Levels

Define clear severity levels.

```yaml
# Alert severity levels
severity_levels:
  P1_CRITICAL:
    description: "Complete service outage or data loss"
    response_time: 15 minutes
    notification: Phone call + SMS + Slack
    escalation: Immediate

  P2_HIGH:
    description: "Major functionality impaired"
    response_time: 30 minutes
    notification: SMS + Slack
    escalation: 30 minutes

  P3_MEDIUM:
    description: "Minor functionality affected"
    response_time: 4 hours
    notification: Slack
    escalation: 4 hours

  P4_LOW:
    description: "Cosmetic or non-urgent issue"
    response_time: Next business day
    notification: Email + ticket
```

### 2. Alerting Rules

Prometheus-style alerting rules.

```yaml
# prometheus/alerts.yml
groups:
  - name: api-service-alerts
    interval: 30s
    rules:
      # Critical alerts
      - alert: ServiceDown
        expr: up{job="api-service"} == 0
        for: 1m
        labels:
          severity: critical
          team: platform
        annotations:
          summary: "API service is down"
          description: "Instance {{ $labels.instance }} has been down for more than 1 minute"
          runbook_url: "https://wiki.example.com/runbooks/service-down"

      - alert: HighErrorRate
        expr: |
          (
            sum(rate(http_requests_total{status_code=~"5.."}[5m]))
            / sum(rate(http_requests_total[5m]))
          ) > 0.05
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          summary: "High HTTP 5xx error rate"
          description: "Error rate is {{ $value | humanizePercentage }} (threshold: 5%)"
          runbook_url: "https://wiki.example.com/runbooks/high-error-rate"

      # Warning alerts
      - alert: HighLatency
        expr: |
          histogram_quantile(0.95,
            sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le)
          ) > 1
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "High API latency detected"
          description: "95th percentile latency is {{ $value }}s (threshold: 1s)"

      - alert: HighMemoryUsage
        expr: |
          (container_memory_usage_bytes / container_memory_limit_bytes) > 0.85
        for: 15m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "High memory usage"
          description: "Memory usage at {{ $value | humanizePercentage }}"

      # Database alerts
      - alert: DatabaseConnectionsHigh
        expr: |
          pg_stat_activity_count / pg_settings_max_connections > 0.8
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "High database connection usage"
          description: "Connection usage at {{ $value | humanizePercentage }}"

      - alert: DatabaseSlowQueries
        expr: |
          rate(pg_stat_statements_mean_exec_time[5m]) > 1000
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "Slow database queries detected"
          description: "Average query execution time is {{ $value }}ms"
```

### 3. SLO-Based Alerts

Alert based on service level objectives.

```yaml
# SLO-based alerting
slo_alerts:
  availability:
    name: "API Availability SLO"
    target: 99.9  # 99.9% availability
    window: 30d
    alert_on_budget_consumption: true
    budget:
      total: 100
      thresholds:
        - percent: 50
          severity: warning
          message: "Availability budget 50% consumed"
        - percent: 75
          severity: critical
          message: "Availability budget 75% consumed - taking action required"
        - percent: 90
          severity: p1
          message: "Availability budget exhausted - immediate action required"

  latency:
    name: "API Latency SLO"
    target: 99  # 99% of requests under 500ms
    window: 30d
    alert_on_budget_consumption: true

# Burn rate alerts
burn_rate_alerts:
  - alert: FastburnAlert
    expr: |
      sum(slo:error-budget-remaining:ratio{slo="api-availability"} < 1)
      and
      (sum(rate(slo:errors-total:slo="api-availability"[1h]))
      / sum(rate(slo:total:slo="api-availability"[1h]))) > 0.1
    for: 15m
    labels:
      severity: critical
    annotations:
      summary: "Fast burn rate detected"
      description: "Error budget is burning fast - 10% of budget in 1 hour"

  - alert: SlowburnAlert
    expr: |
      sum(slo:error-budget-remaining:ratio{slo="api-availability"} < 1)
      and
      (sum(rate(slo:errors-total:slo="api-availability"[6h]))
      / sum(rate(slo:total:slo="api-availability"[6h]))) > 0.01
    for: 1h
    labels:
      severity: warning
```

### 4. Alert Routing

Route alerts to appropriate channels.

```yaml
# AlertManager configuration
global:
  resolve_timeout: 5m

route:
  group_by: ['alertname', 'severity', 'service']
  group_wait: 30s
  group_interval: 5m
  repeat_interval: 4h
  receiver: 'default-receiver'
  routes:
    # Critical alerts - immediate phone call
    - match:
        severity: critical
      receiver: 'pagerduty-critical'
      group_wait: 0s
      repeat_interval: 1h

    # Database alerts
    - match:
        component: database
      receiver: 'database-team'
      routes:
        - match:
            severity: critical
          receiver: 'database-oncall'

    # API alerts
    - match:
        component: api
      receiver: 'api-team'
      routes:
        - match:
            alertname: 'ServiceDown'
          receiver: 'pagerduty-critical'

    # Security alerts - dedicated channel
    - match:
        category: security
      receiver: 'security-team'
      routes:
        - match:
            severity: critical
          receiver: 'security-oncall'

receivers:
  - name: 'default-receiver'
    slack_configs:
      - channel: '#alerts-default'
        send_resolved: true

  - name: 'pagerduty-critical'
    pagerduty_configs:
      - service_key: '${PAGERDUTY_SERVICE_KEY}'
        severity: critical
        send_resolved: true
        client: 'Prometheus'
        client_url: '{{ .CommonLabels.alertmanagerUrl }}'

  - name: 'database-team'
    slack_configs:
      - channel: '#alerts-database'
        send_resolved: true

  - name: 'security-oncall'
    slack_configs:
      - channel: '#alerts-security-critical'
    pagerduty_configs:
      - service_key: '${SECURITY_PAGERDUTY_KEY}'
        severity: critical
```

### 5. Alert Suppression

Prevent alert storms và noise.

```yaml
# Alert suppression rules
suppression:
  # Suppress during maintenance window
  - name: "maintenance-window"
    condition: |
      maintenance_mode == true
    affected_alerts:
      - "HighMemoryUsage"
      - "HighCPUUsage"
      - "HighLatency"

  # Suppress after auto-scaling
  - name: "auto-scaling-in-progress"
    condition: |
      kube_deployment_spec_replicas > kube_deployment_status_replicas
    affected_alerts:
      - "HighCPUUsage"
      - "HighMemoryUsage"
    duration: 10m

  # Acknowledgement based suppression
  - name: "acknowledged-alerts"
    condition: |
      alert_state == "acknowledged"
    affected_alerts:
      - all
    duration: 1h

# Mute schedules
mute_schedules:
  - name: "weekly-maintenance"
    time_intervals:
      - time_range: "saturday 22:00 - sunday 06:00"
        weekdays: ['saturday']
      - time_range: "sunday 00:00 - sunday 06:00"
        weekdays: ['sunday']

  - name: "holiday-mode"
    time_intervals:
      - dates: ['2024-12-25', '2024-12-26', '2024-01-01']
```

### 6. Incident Response

Structured incident handling.

```typescript
// Incident management
interface Incident {
    id: string;
    title: string;
    severity: 'P1' | 'P2' | 'P3' | 'P4';
    status: 'triggered' | 'acknowledged' | 'resolved';
    createdAt: Date;
    acknowledgedAt?: Date;
    resolvedAt?: Date;
    assignee?: string;
    alerts: string[];
    runbook?: string;
    timeline: IncidentEvent[];
}

class IncidentManager {
    async createIncident(alert: Alert): Promise<Incident> {
        const incident: Incident = {
            id: generateIncidentId(),
            title: alert.annotations.summary,
            severity: this.mapSeverity(alert.labels.severity),
            status: 'triggered',
            createdAt: new Date(),
            alerts: [alert.fingerprint],
            runbook: alert.annotations.runbook_url,
            timeline: [{
                timestamp: new Date(),
                event: 'incident_created',
                details: alert
            }]
        };

        await this.incidentStore.save(incident);

        // Auto-assign based on routing
        await this.autoAssign(incident);

        // Send notifications
        await this.notify(incident);

        return incident;
    }

    async acknowledge(incidentId: string, user: string): Promise<void> {
        const incident = await this.incidentStore.findById(incidentId);
        incident.status = 'acknowledged';
        incident.acknowledgedAt = new Date();
        incident.assignee = user;
        incident.timeline.push({
            timestamp: new Date(),
            event: 'incident_acknowledged',
            details: { user }
        });

        await this.incidentStore.save(incident);

        // Update PagerDuty
        await this.pagerduty.acknowledge(incidentId);
    }

    async resolve(incidentId: string, user: string, resolution: string): Promise<void> {
        const incident = await this.incidentStore.findById(incidentId);
        incident.status = 'resolved';
        incident.resolvedAt = new Date();
        incident.timeline.push({
            timestamp: new Date(),
            event: 'incident_resolved',
            details: { user, resolution }
        });

        await this.incidentStore.save(incident);

        // Send resolution notification
        await this.notifyResolution(incident);

        // Close PagerDuty
        await this.pagerduty.resolve(incidentId);
    }
}
```

### 7. Alert Tuning

Reduce noise và improve signal.

```yaml
# Alert tuning process
tuning_guidelines:
  # Too many alerts?
  - check: "Alert frequency > 10/day"
    action: "Review if alerts are actionable"
    possible_issues:
      - "Thresholds too sensitive"
      - "Missing for: clause"
      - "No aggregation"

  # Too few alerts?
  - check: "No alerts for days"
    action: "Review coverage"
    possible_gaps:
      - "Missing SLO-based alerts"
      - "No capacity alerts"
      - "Missing dependency alerts"

# Common tuning adjustments
tuning_examples:
  # Add for clause to prevent flapping
  - before: "alert: HighErrorRate\n  expr: error_rate > 0.01"
    after: "alert: HighErrorRate\n  expr: error_rate > 0.01\n  for: 5m"

  # Aggregate to reduce noise
  - before: "alert: HighErrorRate\n  expr: error_rate{instance=~'.+'}"
    after: "alert: HighErrorRate\n  expr: avg(error_rate) by (service) > 0.01"

  # Add severity-appropriate thresholds
  - before: "alert: HighLatency\n  expr: latency > 500"
    after: |
      alert: HighLatencyWarning
        expr: latency > 500
        for: 5m
        labels: { severity: warning }
      alert: HighLatencyCritical
        expr: latency > 2000
        for: 2m
        labels: { severity: critical }
```

### 8. Runbooks

Documentation for alert response.

```yaml
# Runbook structure
runbook_template: |
  # {{ .AlertName }}

  ## Summary
  {{ .AlertDescription }}

  ## Severity
  {{ .Severity }}

  ## Impact
  - What is affected?
  - Who is impacted?
  - What is the user-visible symptom?

  ## Immediate Actions
  1. Check dashboards: [link]
  2. Verify if this is a real issue
  3. Check recent deployments
  4. Identify affected components

  ## Troubleshooting Steps
  ```bash
  # Check pod status
  kubectl get pods -n {{ .Namespace }}

  # Check pod logs
  kubectl logs -n {{ .Namespace }} {{ .PodName }}

  # Check recent events
  kubectl describe pod -n {{ .Namespace }} {{ .PodName }}
  ```

  ## Possible Causes
  - High traffic
  - Memory leak
  - Database slow queries
  - External dependency failure

  ## Remediation Steps
  1. Scale up if capacity issue
  2. Restart pods if transient issue
  3. Rollback if deployment-related
  4. Engage relevant team

  ## Escalation
  - Primary: {{ .TeamSlack }}
  - Secondary: {{ .OnCall }}
```

### 9. On-Call Rotation

Effective on-call practices.

```yaml
# On-call schedule
oncall:
  schedule:
    rotation_type: weekly
    handoff_time: "09:00 UTC"
    participants:
      - name: Alice
        email: alice@example.com
      - name: Bob
        email: bob@example.com
      - name: Charlie
        email: charlie@example.com

  rotations:
    - name: primary
      current: alice
      schedule: weekly
      escalation_delay: 30m

    - name: secondary
      current: bob
      schedule: weekly
      escalation_delay: 1h

  escalation:
    - level: 1
      timeout: 30m
      contacts: [primary_oncall]
    - level: 2
      timeout: 1h
      contacts: [secondary_oncall, team_lead]
    - level: 3
      contacts: [engineering_manager, vp_engineering]

  policies:
    max_hours_per_week: 40
    min_days_between_shifts: 7
    compensation:
      on_call_stipend: $100/day
      incident_response: $50/incident
```

### 10. Alert Metrics

Track alerting health.

```yaml
# Alert effectiveness metrics
alert_metrics:
  # Volume metrics
  - name: "alerts_total"
    query: sum(rate(alerts_total[5m]))
    description: "Rate of alerts firing"

  - name: "alerts_by_severity"
    query: sum by (severity) (rate(alerts_total[5m]))
    description: "Alerts by severity level"

  # Quality metrics
  - name: "alert_noise_ratio"
    query: |
      sum(rate(alerts_resolved_without_action[5m]))
      / sum(rate(alerts_total[5m]))
    description: "Ratio of noise alerts"

  - name: "mean_time_to_acknowledge"
    query: |
      avg by (alertname) (
        rate(alert_acknowledge_duration_seconds_sum[1h])
        / rate(alert_acknowledge_duration_seconds_count[1h])
      )
    description: "Average time to acknowledge"

  - name: "mean_time_to_resolve"
    query: |
      avg by (alertname) (
        rate(incident_duration_seconds_sum[1h])
        / rate(incident_duration_seconds_count[1h])
      )
    description: "Average time to resolve"

  # SLO metrics
  - name: "error_budget_remaining"
    query: slo:error-budget-remaining:ratio
    description: "Remaining error budget"

  - name: "burn_rate"
    query: slo:current-burn-rate:ratio
    description: "Current error budget burn rate"
```

